## Rejected or deferred sources

Record a source only when the reason for rejection or deferral will prevent weak attribution, invalid transfer, duplication, or repeated search effort. Preserve enough identity information to distinguish it from the selected source.

## Placement rules

- Prefer exact DOI, arXiv, report, dataset, or release identifiers.
- Attach citations to the claims they support; one citation does not automatically support an entire paragraph.
- Use original sources for original results when available, and reviews for synthesis or orientation.
- Do not transfer a result across theories, conventions, profiles, datasets, boundary conditions, or statistical semantics without an explicit assumption map.
- A novelty statement requires a documented search boundary and comparison with the closest primary work.
- Discussion exports, search snippets, and bibliography metadata are not scientific evidence.

## Bibliography gate

Before editing `{{BIB_FILE}}`, verify exact title, authors, persistent identifier, version or release, source type, and duplicate identity. Record the intended claim and manuscript location in the ledger, confirm that assumptions transfer, then rebuild and inspect citation warnings.

